WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.260
[ YouTube Learning ]

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.720
Do you know of a common belief that many teachers

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.320
have about having a YouTube channel?

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.280
Many teachers think that the ONLY reason why they

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.400
should have a YouTube channel is so that they

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.480
could upload their recorded videos to it

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.340
and share it with their students.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:18.590
But that’s not true!

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:21.789
There are many other things you could do with your YouTube channel!

00:00:21.789 --> 00:00:24.140
Let’s understand that in this video.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.300
[ Don't Memorise intro music ]

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.140
We all know that there is a wide variety of

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.220
great quality learning content available on YouTube.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:36.680
And as teachers, we can use these videos to

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.900
teach our students using Google Classroom.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:41.340
Consider this situation where you want to

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.340
create your own collection of videos

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.200
about a particular topic for your students!

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.920
What you need to create then is a PLAYLIST.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.700
It’s nothing but a collection of videos about one topic.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.440
Now you could add your OWN videos to your playlist,

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.920
or you could also add videos created

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.200
by other creators to your playlist.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.510
Let’s focus on the latter here.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:05.390
How do we add other YouTube videos to our playlist?

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:06.810
It’s very easy.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.100
We search for the video first.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:11.700
Once you pick a video, you should watch it

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.780
to make sure it's a good quality video that

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:17.160
is appropriate and relevant for your students to watch...

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:18.960
At the bottom right corner here,

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.960
you will see the “Save” button.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:23.940
Clicking on it will show you this screen.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:26.300
You can then create your new playlist by clicking here,

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:29.400
and then providing a proper name to the playlist.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:33.360
Just like this name, you could have a playlist name like

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.700
eight A math Linear Equations.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:38.540
This playlist will contain all the videos

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:40.540
you curated for this particular chapter.

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.320
You can either keep your playlist public,

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.320
unlisted or private.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.140
If it’s public, it means

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.840
anybody on YouTube will be able to see your playlist.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:52.540
If it’s unlisted, it means only the

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.020
people with your playlist link will be able to see it.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.160
And if it’s private, it means only a few people

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:01.720
you have shared it with will be able to see your playlist.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:04.500
The 2nd and the 3rd options come in handy

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:05.860
when you want only your students

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.420
to watch the videos in your playlist.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:10.500
Let’s keep the playlist public for now.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:13.780
Now if you want to add a second video to your playlist,

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:15.780
then you pick your second video...

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:17.340
click on Save…

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.340
select the playlist...

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:20.720
and it’s done.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:23.680
You can see your playlist on the left here,

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:26.380
and you can always edit or delete your playlist

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:27.980
whenever you feel like.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.420
You can also change the name,

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:31.420
or shuffle the order of videos

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:34.340
or even add a description for your playlist.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.920
When you go back to your channel page by clicking here...

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:38.510
you will see your playlist stored

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:40.560
under the PlayList tab here.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.180
But if it was unlisted or private,

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.180
you wouldn’t see it here.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:49.400
How can I share this playlist with someone else now?

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:52.580
One simple way is by using the right-click option here

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:54.780
and clicking on ‘Copy Link Address’.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.920
To test the link, you could just open a new tab,

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.920
and paste the link in the address bar.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.740
Once this link is pasted in the address bar,

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:05.880
the first video will start playing and you will

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:09.740
see the list of other videos in a sequence on the right.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.700
After the first video ends, YouTube

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:14.520
will automatically start playing the second one.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:18.300
What else could these curated playlists help you with?

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.220
After you conduct a class or a live session,

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:22.800
you could share your playlist

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:23.920
link with your students.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.260
Now that PlayList could cover topics

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.080
that you have taught in your class,

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.340
or the topics that you

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.200
are going to teach in your upcoming class.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.000
With access to videos about the material you teach,

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.720
your students will be able to review

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:37.180
topics at their own pace

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:39.640
and will also be able to bring their doubts

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:41.420
and comments to class.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.360
All of this will immensely improve the

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.360
learning outcomes for your students.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:48.760
But before you start curating videos for your students,

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:50.090
there’s an important thing you

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:52.340
need to know about Searching for videos.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.020
What do most of us do when we want to

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:56.060
search for a video of a particular topic?

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.900
Well, we enter the title in the search bar,

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:01.280
look at the list of videos that appear here,

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:03.380
and select one of them, right?

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:06.680
Have you ever noticed this “Filter” button?

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.600
It can help you filter your search

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.560
based on the parameters you want.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.200
Let’s think of a few examples.

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:15.100
What if you didn’t want to watch the videos

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.280
that were uploaded many years ago?

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:19.820
What if you just wanted to watch the videos

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:23.040
that were recently uploaded in the last 12 months.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:26.820
In order to do that, you just have to click on ‘This year’.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:28.420
And all the videos you see

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:30.420
would have been uploaded in the last 12 months.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.120
So you can select the latest videos

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.560
which will most probably have the latest information

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:36.920
for your students.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:38.920
Sometimes you may want to share an entire

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.700
playlist of videos created by others

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:45.740
with your students or fellow teachers or even friends.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:47.680
Then you just have to click on PlayList

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.680
and you will get access to all the playlists that

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:51.600
the creators have created.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.000
This playlist has 9 videos;

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.280
this one has 19 videos and so on.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:58.580
You can just do a right click here,

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:01.520
copy the link, and share it with whoever you like.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:03.700
Okay, what else?

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:07.000
If you wish to watch short bite-sized videos,

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.000
you can click on this button here.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:10.780
And all the videos you see will be

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.780
less than 4 minutes in length.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.640
What if you want to see videos which have many views?

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:18.280
Then you click on Filter,

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:20.100
and then Sort by Views,

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:21.660
and you will see the list of videos

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:24.020
sorted by the number of views.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:26.060
So the filter button helps you

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:28.060
FILTER the videos that you are looking for!

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:30.420
Okay what else?

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:33.760
As content consumers, we always have preferences.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:37.240
You may like the content delivered by certain channels,

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:39.220
and YouTube gives you this option

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:41.880
to SUBSCRIBE to those channels.

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:44.280
Once you subscribe to your favorite channels,

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.280
whenever they upload videos,

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:48.320
you will be notified of them.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:50.420
And that helps you stay updated.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:53.300
All you need to do is search for the channel you like,

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.620
and click on the Subscribe button here

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:57.360
and then click on the bell icon

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:00.020
to make sure you receive the notifications!

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:02.840
This isn’t the only way though!

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.060
Say you searched for a video and while watching it,

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:08.520
if you end up loving the content, then

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:11.660
you can also click on the Subscribe button you see here.

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:14.380
So these were a couple of ways to subscribe

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:16.380
to your favorite channels on YouTube.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:17.720
Going back to your channel

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:19.080
will show you the list of channels

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.180
you have subscribed to

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:21.680
in the Channels tab here.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.740
It may take some time for them to appear here.

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:27.760
Alternatively, you can also see your subscriptions

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:30.020
here on the left side of the screen.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:33.460
Every time these channels upload videos or share a post,

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:36.760
you will be notified if you’ve clicked on the Bell Icon!

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.580
These are some of the things you can do with your YouTube channel

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:41.979
apart from just uploading videos to it!

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:44.640
In the next video, I will give you tips on

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:46.720
how you can shoot videos at home

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.200
without really investing any money!

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:50.620
See you there!

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:58.080
[ #TeachFromAnywhere ]

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:00.880
[ YouTube Learning ]

